module edge_detect (
    input logic clk,
    input logic rst,
    input logic sig,
    output logic pulse
);
    logic prev;

    always_ff @(posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
        if (rst) begin
            prev <= 1'b0;
            pulse <= 1'b0;
        end else begin
            prev <= sig;
            pulse <= sig & ~prev;
        end
    end
endmodule

### Bug Explanation
The sequential logic uses blocking assignments, so prev is updated before pulse is calculated in the same clock event. That means pulse sees the new value of prev instead of the previous-cycle value, which breaks edge detection. Non-blocking assignments preserve the intended register behavior across clock cycles.

### Verification Suggestion
Hold sig low, then drive it high and confirm pulse goes high for exactly one clock cycle. Keep sig high for additional cycles and verify pulse returns low until the next rising edge.

